---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CtaBand from "../../components/CtaBand.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Our Work"
  description="Forthmark Systems case studies: the live Culia Autos platform, plus clearly labelled concept demonstrations of an operations system and a learning management system."
>
  <header class="page-head">
    <div class="container page-head__grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Our work</p>
        <h1 class="h1">Proof over<br />promises.</h1>
      </div>
      <p class="lede">
        One live client deployment with real product screenshots. Two concept
        demonstrations built to show how we approach common operational problems.
        The distinction is marked on every card and every page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="work-grid">
        <article class="work-card">
          <div class="work-card__media">
            <img
              src="/images/work/culia-public-inventory.png"
              width="1400"
              height="875"
              alt="Culia Autos vehicle inventory page with search filters and car cards showing prices and compare buttons"
              loading="eager"
              decoding="async"
            />
          </div>
          <div class="work-card__body">
            <span class="chip chip--real">Live client project</span>
            <h3>Culia Autos</h3>
            <p>
              A vehicle discovery and consultation platform for a Nigerian car
              dealership. The public site helps buyers browse, save and compare
              cars, then book a paid inspection or consultation. The admin system
              lets the client run inventory, bookings, customer interest and
              payment status without a developer.
            </p>
            <ul class="work-card__list">
              <li>Public website and admin system in one deployment</li>
              <li>Saved cars, comparison and paid consultation booking</li>
              <li>Inventory, reordering, bookings and interest management</li>
            </ul>
            <a class="text-link" href="/work/culia-autos">
              Read the Culia Autos case study
              <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="callout callout--concept mt-3">
        <p>
          <strong>About the concept demonstrations.</strong> The next two projects
          are working software demos, not paid client deployments. They use sample
          businesses, people and records. They exist to make our approach to common
          SME, training and programme operations tangible, and to show the level of
          interaction we design into a system.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid--2 mt-3">
        <article class="concept-card">
          <div
            class="concept-card__shots"
            role="group"
            aria-label="Business operations system screens"
          >
            <figure class="concept-shot">
              <img
                src="/images/work/ops-preview.png"
                width="1400"
                height="900"
                alt="Business operations demo dashboard with revenue, orders and task summaries"
                loading="lazy"
                decoding="async"
              />
              <figcaption>Dashboard</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="concept-shot">
              <img
                src="/images/work/ops-inventory.png"
                width="1400"
                height="900"
                alt="Business operations demo inventory list with stock levels, prices and product records"
                loading="lazy"
                decoding="async"
              />
              <figcaption>Inventory</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="concept-shot">
              <img
                src="/images/work/ops-orders.png"
                width="1400"
                height="900"
                alt="Business operations demo orders view with customer details and status controls"
                loading="lazy"
                decoding="async"
              />
              <figcaption>Orders</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>
          <div class="concept-card__body">
            <span class="chip chip--concept">Concept demonstration</span>
            <h3>Business operations system</h3>
            <p>
              A supply business uses this demo to manage customer records,
              products, stock, orders, tasks and a simple management report.
              Searches, filters, status changes and stock adjustments all work.
            </p>
            <a class="text-link" href="/work/operations-system">
              Open the case study and demo
              <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="concept-card">
          <div
            class="concept-card__shots"
            role="group"
            aria-label="Learning management system screens"
          >
            <figure class="concept-shot">
              <img
                src="/images/work/programme-preview.png"
                width="1400"
                height="900"
                alt="Learning management system demo dashboard showing applications, participants, attendance and certificates"
                loading="lazy"
                decoding="async"
              />
              <figcaption>Dashboard</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="concept-shot">
              <img
                src="/images/work/programme-applications.png"
                width="1400"
                height="900"
                alt="Learning management system applications view with applicant records and status controls"
                loading="lazy"
                decoding="async"
              />
              <figcaption>Applications</figcaption>
            </figure>
            <figure class="concept-shot">
              <img
                src="/images/work/programme-cohorts.png"
                width="1400"
                height="900"
                alt="Learning management system cohorts view with capacity, dates and session schedules"
                loading="lazy"
                decoding="async"
              />
              <figcaption>Cohorts</figcaption>
            </figure>
          </div>
          <div class="concept-card__body">
            <span class="chip chip--concept">Concept demonstration</span>
            <h3>Learning Management System (LMS)</h3>
            <p>
              A training provider uses this demo to review applications,
              manage participants and cohorts, track onboarding and attendance,
              assign tracks, check certificate eligibility and read a summary
              report.
            </p>
            <a class="text-link" href="/work/programme-platform">
              Open the case study and demo
              <span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">&rarr;</span>
            </a>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--paper2">
    <div class="container split">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Evidence standard</p>
        <h2 class="h2">What you see is what was built.</h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <ul class="check-list">
          <li>
            Culia Autos screenshots are taken from the live production website
            and from a local copy of the admin system populated with demo
            records. Personal details and payment references are not shown.
          </li>
          <li>
            The concept demos run in the browser with sample data stored
            locally. They are not connected to a live client account, payment
            provider or third party service.
          </li>
          <li>
            We do not publish invented testimonials, client counts, awards or
            performance metrics.
          </li>
          <li>
            Features that cannot be verified are left out rather than described
            loosely.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CtaBand
    title="Have a process that needs a better system?"
    text="Bring the problem as it is. We will help you decide what to build, what to configure, and what to leave alone."
  />
</BaseLayout>
